{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/972928-time-and-umbra-timetravel-forwards-time","id":972928,"title":"Time and Umbra: Timetravel? (Forwards time)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-19T21:29:59-07:00","id":972928,"title":"Time and Umbra: Timetravel? (Forwards time)","content":"so i was thining a lot about this. i know the umbra follows its own rules when it comes to physics..but after reading a lot about the theory of timetravel (moving faster than light forwards or around a black hole). Is it possible to time travel ? i dont mean back in time to a specific moment. i mean more like &quot;We were gone for two hours.&quot; &quot;an hour there is a year here.&quot; sort of deal. is there any realm's that allow ths kind of effects?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T23:10:03-07:00","id":972952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/972928-time-and-umbra-timetravel-forwards-time#post972928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so i was thining a lot about this. i know the umbra follows its own rules when it comes to physics..but after reading a lot about the theory of timetravel (moving faster than light forwards or around a black hole). Is it possible to time travel ? i dont mean back in time to a specific moment. i mean more like &amp;quot;We were gone for two hours.&amp;quot; &amp;quot;an hour there is a year here.&amp;quot; sort of deal. is there any realm's that allow ths kind of effects?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. The Flux is there most obvious example. One of the Umbra books even had rules for it (and you could go back in time, from memory). It wasn't easy by any means, but it was possible.<br /> But even just in general, going out into the Umbra shouldn't be taken lightly. Once you get further away than the Penumbra, all sorts of phyics shenanigans can happen, as decided by the ST.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T00:03:35-07:00","id":972974,"title":"","content":"I usually use the Umbra to explain any time discrepancies when certain events unfold and I want the PCs there, but they could not possibly make it in time by normal means of transportation.<br /> <br /> And I'm not talking Moonbridge, but rather travel trough the near Umbra or relams and domains, to reach a place...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T04:33:38-07:00","id":973752,"title":"","content":"Agreed with all of the above. Once you leave the penumbra, the &quot;shadow&quot; of earth and reality, the laws of physics have less and less grip on the Umbra. I wouldn't consider it as simple as &quot;You can theoretically travel faster than light and therefore time travel&quot; as much as I'd say &quot;the manner in which time flows relative to Earth is no longer consistent&quot;. So during that two-week hiking trip to visit Rorg in the Asteroid belt, or wandering off to relive some key battle your ancestor fought in WWI in the Battleground.... during certain legs of the trip, what the Garou perceive to be 'forward' in time around them might actually relate to time moving backwards back on Earth, or even ten-times as fast forwards. Maybe they come back yesterday... maybe they come back in 2018.<br /> <br /> Now, obviously those are pretty extreme examples... neither of those probably happen often at all (compared to trips taking days instead of weeks, or weeks instead of days). The most important thing to remember is that the Umbra is generally a realm of ST-control, NOT player. The ST can and should be using it in whatever way they best feel enhances the story, while the players should never (or perhaps as a once-in-a-lifetime epic quest) attempt to directly obtain results from the unpredictability of the Umbra as though it was a basic feature (such as time-travel, teleportation, or the like) rather than a force of nature. They're just as likely to get the opposite of what they were shooting for.<br /> <br /> Lastly, I forget if there was a secondary ability or roll given in the Umbra books for trying to predict, influence, or mitigate this issue in the Umbra... it sounds familiar to me, but that could be some Exalted bleeding into my oWoD memory (there's something to that effect for navigating the Underworld, I believe).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T11:26:52-07:00","id":973942,"title":"","content":"My homebrew idea is there are demiplanes, the uchronies, like parallel earth or alternate timelines. They can travel to a &quot;clone past&quot; but not to change thir own past. You could find a wold ruled by creatures from &quot;Kult: lost divintiy&quot;, a zombie post-apocalypse, with dinosaurs, or Great Alexander self-proclaimed prophet. <br /> <br /> Do remeber Earth doesn't spin around the sun, but also sun is spining around the galaxy. The true movement of the planets is more like a spring than a ellipse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T22:50:59-07:00","id":978875,"title":"","content":"So, WAY back in the 90s, White Wolf licensed their Rage CCG to Five Rings Publishing Group, and they came out with &quot;RAGE Across Las Vegas: Snake Eyes&quot;.<br /> In it, FRPG had said that the Glass Walkers had developed time travel to go back to the Wild West (they also had control over Area 51 and were splicing Werewolf DNA with Alien DNA... I shit you not.)<br /> I was actually helping FRPG demo the game when Luke P. told me this. I went immediately to the White Wolf booth to confront them with this and their reply was: &quot;Yeah, no, that's not canon for our game. That's something they came up with on their own. You should have heard what else they wanted to do. I guess, for us, you could think of it like 'it's not really the Wild West, but a realm they're going to and only think it's the past&quot;.&quot; So, yeah, even to White Wolf, the idea of true time-travel wasn't something they were keen on (at least under the storytelling of FRPG.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T00:01:49-07:00","id":978894,"title":"","content":"The time travel is a illusion. You can't really change the past, but to create a &quot;Sch\u00f6ringer's effect&quot;. How to expalin it better? Let's imagine a experiment. The chrononaut goes to the past to cut a tree in a laboratory and come backs to the present. How is the tree, cutted or full? Both at same time. Like a hologram you can see the tree is &quot;normal&quot;, but you move and the tree is &quot;broken&quot;. The most of people would be a normal tree, but some special people could be the cutted. They reality would try to hide the most radical changes. <br /> <br /> Other option could be travelling to parallel earths, where the changes in the second timeline wouldn't affect (or almost) the original timeline by the chrononaut.<br /> <br /> I guess the mokole would be the keepers of those time-travel cosmic gates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}